		"Node.js globals and modules such as `global`, `process`, `require`, `module`, `fs` / `node:fs`, `child_process`, `http`, `https`, `net`, `fetch`, `Worker`, `Buffer`, `Electron`, `Bun`, and `Deno` are not Code Mode language globals. Use the documented tools.* APIs or tools.execute_terminal for host operations instead.",
		"Unsupported executable language/runtime constructs are rejected before tool execution so they cannot cause a partial tools.* mutation. Non-executable literal text such as strings, comments, regex literals, and template-literal text may still contain those names.",
